const body=`Decision closed after declaration-level audits of all three routes.

SELECT R1, with its finite-field completion made explicit: implement the coordinate-twist atlas over an infinite/large field, then descend across a finite Galois extension K/k chosen so |P^1(K)| > g. This is the only route that preserves the landed DD-R window, epsilon, classifier, and representing-scheme architecture.

REJECT R2 as the primary route: the cited Stacks tag 0B8B is unrelated; 0B9A/0B9B only give fibrewise affine neighbourhoods. LocalEquations has no finite support morphism, and a usable framed-cover generalisation reaches about 60 files (theta frames, flatness, pullback, cocycles, classifier).

REJECT R3 as the primary route: no native finite-flat Cartier-divisor carrier or bridge exists; it would replace the representation layer, while the sibling Quot route still contains admitted representability and lacks the required rank-g support theorem.

R1's remaining obligations are therefore (1) finite-set fibre avoidance with its honest cardinal hypothesis, (2) a twist-indexed local atlas rather than a false fixed-pi equivalence, and (3) finite-Galois/fppf descent for small finite fields.`;
const r1=await tools.exec_command({cmd:`horizon roadmap comment AJCR.w4-rep.datum.dat-d.ddr.certificate.widen-decision --body ${JSON.stringify(body)} --author horizon --json`,workdir:"/home/axel/LeanAlgebraicGeometry-Horizon",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:12000});
const r2=await tools.exec_command({cmd:"horizon roadmap set AJCR.w4-rep.datum.dat-d.ddr.certificate.widen-decision --status done --author horizon --json",workdir:"/home/axel/LeanAlgebraicGeometry-Horizon",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:12000});
text(r1.output);text(r2.output);

